1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:02,480
Here's how to write a note in Tidepool,

2
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:05,051
tag it, and find it again in seconds.

3
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:08,490
Click New note, and type a title.

4
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:10,420
Press Enter to move to the body,

5
00:00:10,420 --> 00:00:11,679
and start writing.

6
00:00:12,139 --> 00:00:14,994
Tidepool saves it on
this device as you type.

7
00:00:16,273 --> 00:00:19,013
To tag it, click the tag
field under the title.

8
00:00:19,133 --> 00:00:21,314
Type a tag, and press Enter.

9
00:00:21,764 --> 00:00:24,358
The new tag shows up in the sidebar, too.

10
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:26,949
Later, from any note,

11
00:00:26,949 --> 00:00:28,260
press Command K,

12
00:00:28,260 --> 00:00:30,000
and type a word from the note.

13
00:00:30,190 --> 00:00:32,173
Matches light up as you type.

14
00:00:32,543 --> 00:00:34,803
Press Enter to jump straight back to it.

15
00:00:35,963 --> 00:00:37,833
To list every note with a tag,

16
00:00:37,833 --> 00:00:39,596
start the search with a hash.

17
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:45,813
New note. A tag. Command K.

18
00:00:46,163 --> 00:00:47,503
That's the whole loop.
